1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://dbpedia-live.openlinksw.com/page/Maria_Eleonora_I_Boncompagni dbpedia - '''Maria Elenora I Boncompagni''']
2 CONT * Maria Eleonora I Boncompagni (1686–1745) was the Princess of Piombino, Marchioness of Populonia, Princess of Venosa and Countess of Conza, Lady di Scarlino, Populonia, Vignale, Abbadia del Fango, Suvereto, Buriano, Isola d’Elba,
2 CONC  Montecristo, Pianosa, Cerboli e Palmaiolan, from 1733 until her death. She was the oldets of six daughters to her mother Ippolita Ludovisi. She succeeded her mother as sovereign at her death in 1733.
2 CONT * She was '''married to her uncle''', '''Don Antonio I Boncompagni''', who became Prince of Piombino by the right of his wife (1658-1721).
