1 OCCU actress, writer, radio announcer, television personality, game-show panellist, animal rights activist
1 TITL Donna
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Katie Boyle, Lady Saunders (born Caterina Irene Elena Maria Imperiali di Francavilla; 29 May 1926 – 20 March 2018) was an Italian-born British actress, television personality, and game-show panelist, well known for
2 CONC  appearing on TV panel games such as What's My Line? and for presenting the Eurovision Song Contest four times in the 1960s and 1970s. She was once an agony aunt, answering problems that had been posted to the TV Times by readers.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Florence, Tuscany, Italy, the daughter of an Italian marquis (the Marchese Demetrio Imperiali di Francavilla), and his English wife, Dorothy Kate Ramsden. She came to Great Britain in 1946.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1947 she married Richard Bentinck Boyle, heir to the 8th Earl of Shannon; the marriage was dissolved in 1955 but she kept his surname (Boyle). Later that year she married Greville Baylis, a racehorse owner, who died in 1976. In
2 CONC  1979, she married theatre impresario Sir Peter Saunders, who died in 2003
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Katie_Boyle
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine I E Boyle
2 CONT * England & Wales, Marriage Index, 1837-2005
2 CONT * Marriage date:	July-Aug-Sep 1955
2 CONT * Marriage place:	Chelsea, London, England
2 CONT * Spouse (implied):	Greville P Baylis
