1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Francesco Barberini was Italian Cardinal of the family of Pope Urban VIII (1623–1644) and of Princes of Palestrina.
2 CONT
2 CONT A member of the Barberini family, he was the eldest son of Maffeo Barberini and Olimpia Giustiniani (a niece of Pope Innocent X), the nephew of cardinal Carlo Barberini and the grandson of Taddeo Barberini (a nephew of Pope Urban 
2 CONC VIII). He gave up his birthright (as eldest son) for an ecclesiastic career thereby making his brother, Urbano Barberini, heir to the Barberini estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created by Pope Alexander VIII on 13 November 1690 with the dispensation of having a cousin (Rinaldo d'Este, who later left his ecclesiastic career to marry) and uncle (Carlo Barberini) in the Sacred College and for not hav
2 CONC ing yet received the minor orders.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was ordained deacon only in 1700 and priest in 1715. He participated in the five papal conclaves (1691, 1700, 1721, 1724 and 1730). Abbot of Farfa and Subiaco from 1704. He was Cardinal-Bishop of Palestrina (March 3, 1721 until
2 CONC  July 1, 1726) and Cardinal-Bishop of Ostia e Velletri (July 1, 1726). Prefect of the Sacred Congregations of Bishops and Regulars and of Waters from 1726. Dean of the Sacred College of Cardinals in December 1734.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at his Roman palace, at the age of 75.
