1 OCCU Ambasciatore per la Repubblica di Genova alla corte di Filippo II di Spagna
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He held prominent positions both in Genoa as well as throughout the Italian peninsula and Europe. His wife, Mariettina Sauli, granted him important ties to the Vatican that initiated his involvement in the Genoese 
2 CONC alum trade. In 1543 Luca joined with Tobia Pallavicino to form a banking venture whose shareholders were the primary Genoese alum traders. He also oversaw the shipping of alum to Venice between 1541 and 1548. Luca also served as a
2 CONC  diplomat for various powerful groups: from 1538 to 1542 and in 1544 he performed the duties of provincial papal treasurer. He distributed income to functionaries and soldiers in addition to overseeing funding for the construction
2 CONC  and repair o fortresses and other government buildings. He was Genoese ambassador to Parma and Piacenza.
