2 CONT
2 CONT Kieran Owens, 27/02/2021 20:36 Another son of Ersinia Caetani-Lovatelli was Commander Count Giovanni Lovatelli, of the Italian battleship 'Roma'. The Portsmouth Evening News, of Thursday 2nd February 1911, reported that he was the
2 CONC  only Italian officer to be awarded the Victoria Cross, for saving the life of the British Consul at Zanzibar (though I can find no reference to his receiving this award). He was formerly naval attaché to the Italian Embassy in Lo
2 CONC ndon, was a Knight of Malta, and was created C.M.G. (Hon) (Companion of Most Distinguished Order of Saint Michael and Saint George) in December 1893. It is not impossible that through his diplomatic associations his brother Filipp
2 CONC o might have had a connection to Sir John G. Kennedy.
