1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/175764603/person/152281434504 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 4 2021, 18:25:42 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.artuk.org/artdetective/discussions/discussions/can-you-tell-us-more-about-the-sculptor-filippo-lovatelli
2 CONT
2 CONT Kieran Owens, 26/02/2021 21:40 Other sources indicate that his father was Giacomo, Count Lovatelli (1832 - 1879) and his mother was Ersinia Caetani-Lovatelli (née di Sermoneta (1840 - Rome, 22nd December 1925), the daughter of Mic
2 CONC hael Angelo, Duke of Sermoneta. Also know as Philipp, he married Adelaide Keen Vargas, of Azul Partido, Argentina (1879 - ), and they had one son, Loffredo, Count Gaetani dell' Aquila d'Aragona Lovatelli (Rome, 22nd April 1912 - 3
2 CONC 1 JAN 1992 • Argiano, Siena, Tuscany, Italy, 31st January 1992).
2 CONT
2 CONT In February 1922 he was badly wounded in a duel with swords in Rome with Don Martino Torlonia when the latter's wife refused to pay the artist £5,000 for a bust of herself, offering only €200 instead (or, as reported elsewhere, $2
2 CONC 5,000 and $1,000).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was still alive in 1934, living on the Argiano estate, in the municipality of Montalcino (Siena).
2 CONT
2 CONT Lovatelli was responsible for the Kennedy Brothers' mural monument memorial in Holy Trinity Church, Cuckfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT From his address at via Maria Christina, 5, Rome, this Discussion's bust was exhibited as item no. 1405 by Lovatelli at the 1924 Royal Academy exhibition. The catalogue entry read:
2 CONT
2 CONT "1405 - Ginie Courtauld - half figure, marble - Filippo Locatelli"
